test/hardware/WiiLibProbe on a Seeed XIAO SAMD21 (Seeeduino SAMD core 1.8.6,
arduino-cli 1.5.1), NintendoExtensionCtrl 0.8.3, a genuine Nunchuk on
Adafruit's Wii Nunchuck Breakout Adapter with VIN on the XIAO's 3V3,
2026-10-29. The probe's serial output at 115200, read for set times by a short
Python script (the capture) and copied here from the record of the session
that ran it, its CR LF line ends made LF. The capture added the "---" lines,
the "run N:", "s |" and "f |" prefixes and the "status lines before the
test:" line, and in the scan section kept only the probe's lines that start
"scan" or "0x52", joined by " || ". The "==" headings and the lines marked
[the capture] are added here. Times are UTC, when each section's output came
back.

The probe grew between sections: the clock section ran on its first build,
the scan section once 'q' and its 0x52 rounds were added, the identity
section once 'i' was. Each build only added code and comments to the one
before, so what ran in each section is unchanged in WiiLibProbe.ino as
committed, whose code is the build the identity section ran.

A status line comes once a second and counts the calls since the line before:
connect() and update() that succeeded / were made, the type the library names
and the six bytes of control data it holds (getControlData(); connect()
zeroes them). Its clock is the one in force when it prints, so the line
printed in the second a clock change falls in counts calls at both clocks.

